          "line": 4,
          "text": "description: \"SGLang multi-LoRA serving: S-LoRA and Punica techniques, dynamic adapter loading, GPU pinning, overlap loading, Triton and CSGMV backends.\""
        },
        {
          "line": 6,
          "text": "SGLang enables the use of [LoRA adapters](https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.09685) with a base model. By incorporating techniques from [S-LoRA](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2311.03285) and [Punica](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2310.18547), S"
        },
        {
          "line": 9,
          "text": "## Arguments for LoRA Serving"
        },
        {
          "line": 12,
          "text": "The following server arguments are relevant for multi-LoRA serving:"
        },
        {
          "line": 14,
          "text": "* `enable_lora`: Enable LoRA support for the model. This argument is automatically set to True if `--lora-paths` is provided for backward compatibility."
        },
        {
          "line": 16,
          "text": "* `enable_lora_overlap_loading`: Enable asynchronous LoRA weight loading in order to overlap H2D transfers with GPU compute. This should be enabled if you find that your LoRA workloads are bottlenecked by adapter weight "
        },
        {
          "line": 18,
          "text": "* `lora_paths`: The list of LoRA adapters to load. Each adapter must be specified in one of the following formats: &lt;PATH&gt; | &lt;NAME&gt;=&lt;PATH&gt; | JSON with schema &#123;\"lora_name\":str,\"lora_path\":str,\"pinned"
        },
        {
          "line": 20,
          "text": "* `max_loras_per_batch`: Maximum number of adaptors used by each batch. This argument can affect the amount of GPU memory reserved for multi-LoRA serving, so it should be set to a smaller value when memory is scarce. Def"
        },
        {
          "line": 22,
          "text": "* `max_loaded_loras`: If specified, it limits the maximum number of LoRA adapters loaded in CPU memory at a time. The value must be greater than or equal to `max-loras-per-batch`."
        },
        {
          "line": 24,
          "text": "* `lora_eviction_policy`: LoRA adapter eviction policy when GPU memory pool is full. `lru`: Least Recently Used (default, better cache efficiency). `fifo`: First-In-First-Out."
        },
        {
          "line": 26,
          "text": "* `lora_backend`: The backend of running GEMM kernels for Lora modules. Currently we support Triton LoRA backend (`triton`) and Chunked SGMV backend (`csgmv`). In the future, faster backend built upon Cutlass or Cuda ker"
        }
      ],
